/** @page xmlsoapguide SOAP and WSDL Web Services

    @tableofcontents

    The user modules delivered with the xml module implement SOAP 1.1 and SOAP 1.2 web services described by WSDL
    1.1 documents: clients, a server handler and data providers share one model of the service, built by the
    @ref wsdlintro "WSDL" module from the WSDL document and its XML schemas.

    @section xmlsoapmodules Choosing a Module

    |!Task|!Module|!Main class
    |Call a SOAP service (asynchronous I/O, HTTP/3, HTTP/2 or HTTP/1.1, connection pooling; recommended)|\
        @ref soapclientiointro "SoapClientIo"|@ref SoapClientIo::SoapClientIo "SoapClientIo"
    |Call a SOAP service with the synchronous \c HTTPClient API|@ref soapclientintro "SoapClient"|\
        @ref SoapClient::SoapClient "SoapClient"
    |Serve SOAP operations from the %Qore \c HttpServer|@ref soaphandlerintro "SoapHandler"|\
        @ref SoapHandler::SoapHandler "SoapHandler"
    |Introspect and call SOAP operations through the data provider API|\
        @ref soapdataproviderintro "SoapDataProvider"|@ref SoapDataProvider::SoapDataProvider "SoapDataProvider"
    |Call the Salesforce SOAP APIs|@ref salesforcesoapclientintro "SalesforceSoapClient"|\
        @ref SalesforceSoapClient::SalesforceSoapClient "SalesforceSoapClient"
    |Parse WSDL documents and schemas, and serialize or parse SOAP messages without a transport|\
        @ref wsdlintro "WSDL"|@ref WSDL::WebService "WebService"

    Connection objects for the clients are provided as well (\c soap, \c soaps and \c sfsoap schemes), so services
    can be configured as %Qore connections.

